      "Definition": "A macrocytic normochromic anemia characterized by delayed nuclear maturation relative to cytoplasmic development (nuclear-cytoplasmic asynchrony) in erythroblasts due to defective DNA synthesis, caused by Vitamin B12 or Folic Acid deficiency. Pernicious anemia specifically refers to Vitamin B12 deficiency resulting from gastric mucosal atrophy and failure of Intrinsic Factor (IF) secretion.",
