      "Clinical Features / Signature Symptoms": "- General: Pallor, lemon-yellow skin tint (anemia + mild jaundice from intramedullary hemolysis), weakness, sore beefy red tongue (Hunter's glossitis).\n- Neurological (B12 specific): Paresthesias in extremities, loss of vibration and position sense, spastic ataxia, positive Romberg sign.\n- Signature Sign: **Hypersegmented neutrophils** (neutrophils displaying 6 or more nuclear lobes) on peripheral blood smear.",
