      "Drugs": "Corticosteroids (Prednisolone), Folic acid, Recombinant EPO (in renal complications).",
      "Receptors / Channels / Transporters": "Fc receptors and C3b receptors on splenic macrophages, Haptoglobin, Hemopexin.",
      "Equations / Relationships": "Heme -> Biliverdin (via Heme Oxygenase) -> Unconjugated Bilirubin (via Biliverdin Reductase).",
      "Differential Diagnosis": "Hereditary Spherocytosis vs Autoimmune Hemolytic Anemia (Coombs negative vs positive), G6PD deficiency, Microangiopathic Hemolytic Anemia.",
      "Complications": "Pigment gallstones (bilirubin lithiasis), acute tubular necrosis, high-output heart failure, iron overload (hemosiderosis)."
