      "Name with Synonyms": "Polycythemia Vera (PV), Polycythemia Rubra Vera, Primary Polycythemia, Erythremia.",
      "Definition": "A chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm characterized by autonomous, uncontrolled clonal proliferation of hematopoietic stem cells in the bone marrow, leading to excessive production of erythrocytes, granulocytes, and platelets independent of erythropoietin regulation.",
      "Normal Physiology": "Normal erythropoiesis is strictly regulated by erythropoietin (EPO), produced by renal peritubular interstitial cells in response to tissue hypoxia. EPO binds EPO-receptors on CFU-E progenitors, activating the JAK2 (Janus Kinase 2) signaling pathway to promote survival and division.",
