      "Pathophysiology": "Endothelial damage or vascular stasis initiates platelet adhesion and aggregation. Platelet factor release accelerates localized prothrombin activator formation, generating thrombin and converting fibrinogen into a fibrin mesh. The growing clot entraps blood cells, creating an intravascular thrombus that narrows or occludes the lumen.",
