      "Definition": "A severe hemolytic disease of the fetus and newborn child characterized by agglutination and phagocytosis of fetal red blood cells due to maternal-fetal blood group incompatibility.",
      "Normal Physiology": "Human red blood cells express surface membrane proteins called blood group antigens (agglutinogens), including the ABO and Rh (D antigen) systems. Rh-positive individuals express the Rh antigen, whereas Rh-negative individuals do not. Anti-Rh antibodies (agglutinins) are not naturally occurring in human plasma but develop in an Rh-negative person after exposure to Rh-positive blood.",
