      "Clinical Features / Signature Symptoms": "Severe anemia, hemolytic jaundice, generalized systemic edema (Hydrops Fetalis), and major motor/neurological deficits (Kernicterus).",
      "Physiological Basis of Features": "- Anemia: Caused by direct immune destruction and accelerated clearance of antibody-coated fetal erythrocytes by maternal IgG anti-Rh antibodies.\n- Jaundice: Massive hemoglobin degradation yields excessive biliverdin and unconjugated bilirubin, overwhelming neonatal liver conjugation capacity.\n- Hydrops Fetalis: Widespread fetal tissue edema resulting from a combination of severe heart failure secondary to tissue hypoxia/anemia and hypoproteinemia (reduced plasma oncotic pressure).\n- Kernicterus: Deposition of lipid-soluble unconjugated bilirubin in the basal ganglia (which have a high affinity for bilirubin) because the immature neonatal blood-brain barrier is permeable.",
