      "Physiological Basis of Features": "- Severe Chest Pain: Prolonged ischemia causes accumulation of acidic metabolic byproducts (lactic acid) and \"P factor\" (potassium) that stimulate visceral sensory pain fibers in the myocardium.\n- Radiation to Left Arm: Sensory afferent fibers from the heart enter upper thoracic spinal cord segments (T1–T4) that overlap with somatic sensory input from the ulnar nerve distribution of the left arm (referred pain).\n- Diaphoresis: Intense activation of the sympathoadrenal medullary axis triggered by severe pain and circulatory stress.\n- Bradycardia & Hypotension: Chemical substances released from infarcted tissue activate ventricular chemoreceptors, triggering the Bezold-Jarisch reflex (coronary chemoreflex).",
