      "Physiological Basis of Features": "- Harsh Systolic Murmur & Thrill: Blood jets at tremendous velocity through the small fibrous opening, creating severe turbulence in the aortic root that strongly vibrates the thoracic wall.\n- Anacrotic Pulse: Ejection obstruction slows the rate of blood entry into the systemic arterial tree, producing a slow, sloping pulse upstroke with a secondary wave.\n- Angina Pectoris: Hypertrophied myocardium has an increased oxygen demand, while high intraventricular wall tension and reduced aortic lateral pressure impair subendocardial coronary perfusion.\n- Exertional Dyspnea: Increased venous return during exercise accentuates left ventricular pressure overload, rapidly backing blood up into the lungs.",
