      "Site": "Systemic circulation and microvascular capillary beds.",
      "Pathophysiology": "- Acute blood/fluid loss decreases mean systemic filling pressure, diminishing venous return to the heart.\n- Decreased end-diastolic volume lowers stroke volume and cardiac output via the Frank-Starling mechanism.\n- Arterial hypotension unloads high-pressure baroreceptors, triggering intense sympathetic nervous system stimulation.\n- Sympathetic activity induces selective arteriolar vasoconstriction (diverting flow to brain and heart), venoconstriction, and tachycardia.\n- Decreased capillary hydrostatic pressure causes transcapillary fluid absorption from interstitial spaces into blood vessels.\n- Renal hypoperfusion activates RAAS and ADH release, suppressing urine output to conserve fluid.",
