      "Physiological Basis of Features": "- Hypotension: Inadequate blood volume reducing cardiac output.\n- Tachycardia & Thready Pulse: Reflex baroreceptor-mediated sympathetic stimulation and adrenal medullary catecholamine release acting on cardiac beta-1 receptors.\n- Cold & Pale Skin: Sympathetic alpha-1 mediated cutaneous vasoconstriction, conserving blood flow for vital organs (brain and heart).\n- Tachypnea: Rapid breathing driven by hypoxia/metabolic acidosis, which also enhances the \"thoracic pump\" to assist venous return.\n- Intense Thirst: Hypovolemia and hyperosmolality triggering hypothalamic thirst centers.\n- Oliguria & Azotemia: Sympathetic renal vasoconstriction and low blood pressure decrease GFR; ADH and aldosterone promote maximum tubular reabsorption of water and salt, retaining nitrogenous waste products in the blood.",
