      "Pathophysiology": "Mechanical factors restrict ventricular relaxation in diastole or impede ventricular ejection in systole. Restriction of ventricular expansion causes a drastic fall in end-diastolic volume (EDV). By the Frank-Starling law, reduced EDV impairs myocardial stroke volume and cardiac output. Upstream pressure rises, leading to systemic or pulmonary venous congestion, while arterial blood pressure falls.",
