      "Physiological Basis of Features": "- Hypotension: Marked drop in stroke volume and cardiac output due to restricted ventricular diastolic filling.\n- Elevated JVP: Backward damming of venous blood into systemic veins because blood cannot freely enter compressed right cardiac chambers.\n- Cold, Pale Skin: Baroreceptor-mediated reflex sympathetic vasoconstriction diverting remaining blood flow away from the cutaneous bed to vital organs (brain and heart).\n- Pulsus Paradoxus: Exaggerated decrease in systemic arterial pulse amplitude and systolic BP (> 10 mmHg) during inspiration caused by inspiratory pooling of blood in pulmonary vessels combined with limited ventricular expansion space within the compressed thoracic/pericardial cavity.",
