      "Physiological Basis of Features": "- Expiratory Wheezing / Dyspnea: During inspiration, negative intrapleural pressure pulls airways open, allowing air entry; during expiration, positive thoracic pressure compresses the partially occluded bronchioles, producing severe expiratory obstruction, high-velocity turbulence, and wheezing.\n- Air Trapping / Barrel Chest: Expiratory airflow obstruction prevents complete emptying, acutely increasing FRC and RV during attacks; over years, repeated hyperinflation permanently enlarges the chest cage.",
