      "Treatment + Physiological Basis": "- Nasal CPAP (Continuous Positive Airway Pressure): Administers continuous positive pressure air via a nasal mask to create a pneumatic stent that keeps upper airway passages open during inspiration.\n- Surgical Interventions: Uvulopalatopharyngoplasty (UPPP) or tonsillectomy to excise obstructing soft tissues, or tracheostomy to bypass the upper airway.",
