      "Normal Physiology": "Deglutition triggers a primary peristaltic wave along the esophagus. Ahead of the peristaltic wave, the myenteric plexus releases non-adrenergic non-cholinergic (NANC) inhibitory neurotransmitters—specifically Nitric Oxide (NO) and Vasoactive Intestinal Polypeptide (VIP)—inducing receptive relaxation of the LES to allow food passage into the stomach.",
