      "Definition": "Inflammation of the gastric mucosa, ranging from superficial irritation to deep mucosal atrophy and ulcerative excoriation.",
      "Normal Physiology": "The gastric mucosal barrier consists of a viscous gel layer (~0.2 mm thick) secreted by mucous cells containing mucin, phospholipids, electrolytes, and bicarbonate ( HCO_3- ). This layer creates an alkaline mucosal surface (pH ~7.0) that shields epithelial cells from highly acidic gastric juice (pH 1.0–2.0, where H+ concentration is ~100,000 times higher than in plasma).",
