      "Etiology": "1. Post-operative state (excessive handling/trauma of intestines during abdominal surgery).\n2. Peritonitis (inflammation of the peritoneal cavity).\n3. Electrolyte disturbances (hypokalemia or hyperkalemia).\n4. Metabolic disorders (ketoacidosis, uremia).\n5. Intestinal ischemia, intra-abdominal hemorrhage, renal colic.\n6. Drugs (anticholinergics, opioids).",
