      "Treatment + Physiological Basis": "- Conservative Management: Nasogastric suction/decompression (removes accumulated gas and fluid); intravenous fluids and electrolyte correction (restores intravascular volume and corrects hypokalemia to restore smooth muscle excitability); \"NPO\" (nil per os).\n- Discontinuation of Offending Drugs: Stop anticholinergics or opioids.\n- Addressing Underlying Cause: Medical or surgical treatment of peritonitis or metabolic disorders.",
      "Drugs": "Intravenous isotonic crystalloids, potassium chloride replacement, prokinetic agents (neostigmine).",
      "Receptors / Channels / Transporters": "_2 and _2 adrenergic receptors (mediating sympathetic smooth muscle inhibition), M_3 muscarinic receptors (mediating parasympathetic stimulation).",
      "Differential Diagnosis": "Mechanical Intestinal Obstruction (characterized by high-pitched, hyperactive bowel sounds / \"tinkling\" rushes and severe cramping colicky pain, rather than a silent abdomen).",
      "Complications": "Hypovolemic shock, severe electrolyte imbalances, intestinal wall ischemia, bowel perforation, and sepsis."
