      "Normal vs. Abnormal Values": "Normal fecal fat excretion = < 5 g/24 hours; in celiac disease, fecal fat > 7–20 g/day. Normal 5-hr urinary D-xylose excretion = > 4.5 g; in celiac disease, D-xylose excretion is markedly reduced (< 3 g).",
