      "Etiology": "1. Hemolytic (Prehepatic) Jaundice: Excessive intravascular or extravascular RBC destruction (sickle cell anemia, hereditary spherocytosis, G6PD deficiency, immune hemolysis, incompatible transfusion).\n2. Hepatic (Hepatocellular) Jaundice: Hepatocyte damage or impaired conjugation/excretion (viral hepatitis, toxic liver injury, cirrhosis, neonatal physiological jaundice due to immature glucuronyl transferase).\n3. Obstructive (Posthepatic / Cholestatic) Jaundice: Obstruction of bile outflow (gallstones in common bile duct, biliary strictures, carcinoma of head of pancreas).",
