      "Clinical Features / Signature Symptoms": "Yellowish discoloration of sclera and skin.\n- Hemolytic: Mild jaundice, dark-brown stools (high stercobilin), normal-colored urine (no urinary bilirubin / acholuric), splenomegaly.\n- Hepatic: Moderate jaundice, dark yellow urine, variable stool color, malaise, anorexia.\n- Obstructive: Severe deep-yellow/greenish jaundice, **clay-colored (pale) stools**, **deep yellow/tea-colored urine** (foams yellow), generalized **pruritus** (itching due to skin deposition of retained bile salts), and steatorrhea.",
