      "Physiological Basis of Features": "- Ascites & Generalized Edema: Dual mechanism: (1) Fibrotic compression of portal venous drainage elevates portal capillary hydrostatic pressure, and (2) failure of hepatocytes to synthesize albumin drops plasma colloid osmotic pressure (oncotic pressure), driving fluid transudation into the peritoneal cavity.\n- Gynecomastia & Spider Nevi: Impaired hepatic degradation and clearance of circulating estrogens.\n- Bleeding Tendencies: Impaired hepatic synthesis of clotting factors (fibrinogen, prothrombin/II, VII, IX, X) and Vitamin K malabsorption.\n- Hepatic Encephalopathy: Portosystemic shunting bypasses liver filtration, allowing toxic gut-derived nitrogenous substances (ammonia) to enter systemic circulation and cross the blood-brain barrier.",
