      "Clinical Features / Signature Symptoms": "**Esophageal varices** (enlarged submucosal veins at the gastroesophageal junction), **Hematemesis** (vomiting bright red blood or coffee-ground material from variceal rupture), **Melena**, **Splenomegaly** (enlarged spleen), **Caput Medusae** (distended, engorged cutaneous veins radiating from the umbilicus), Rectal varices (hemorrhoids), and **Ascites**.",
