      "Definition": "An abrupt, sudden, but usually reversible deterioration in renal function occurring within hours or a few days, characterized by a rapid decline in Glomerular Filtration Rate (GFR), accumulation of nitrogenous waste products (azotemia), and usually a reduction in urine output.",
