      "Etiology": "- Prerenal AKI: Decreased renal blood flow/underperfusion without parenchymal damage, caused by severe hemorrhage, hypovolemic shock, dehydration, or congestive heart failure.\n- Intrarenal (Intrinsic) AKI: Abnormalities within the renal parenchyma affecting blood vessels, glomeruli, or tubules; most commonly caused by Acute Tubular Necrosis (ATN) due to ischemia, toxic drugs, hemoglobinuria (mismatched transfusion), or rhabdomyolysis/myoglobinuria.\n- Postrenal AKI: Mechanical obstruction of the urinary collecting system anywhere from the renal calyces to the urethra, caused by kidney stones, prostatic enlargement, or retroperitoneal tumors.",
