      "Treatment + Physiological Basis": "- Treatment of Underlying Cause: Discontinue offending medications; replace thyroxine in hypothyroidism.\n- Dopamine Receptor Agonists (Cabergoline / Bromocriptine): Directly inhibits anterior pituitary prolactin secretion, halting lactogenesis and causing rapid cessation of galactorrhea.\n- Avoidance of Breast Stimulation: Stopping self-examination and mechanical friction that maintains neural reflex release of prolactin.",
