      "Etiology": "1. Prolonged exogenous administration of glucocorticoids for therapeutic purposes (most common overall, iatrogenic).\n2. Adrenal cortical tumors (adenomas or carcinomas) secreting cortisol autonomously.\n3. Ectopic secretion of ACTH or CRH by non-pituitary tumors (e.g., bronchogenic carcinoma).\n4. Pituitary ACTH-producing adenomas (specifically termed Cushing's Disease).",
