      "Clinical Features / Signature Symptoms": "Sustained or paroxysmal **hypertension**, accompanied by the classic hyperadrenergic spells/triad of severe **headache**, **palpitations** (forceful heartbeat), and **excessive sweating (diaphoresis)**. Additional features include severe anxiety/feeling of impending death, chest and epigastric pain, dyspnea, tremors, pallor, and orthostatic hypotension in chronic cases.",
