      "Diagnostic / Physiological Tests": "- Co-estimation of Intact PTH and Serum Calcium: High PTH accompanied by low or normal serum calcium confirms secondary hyperparathyroidism.\n- Renal Function Tests (BUN, Serum Creatinine): Confirms underlying chronic renal disease.\n- Serum 25-OH and 1,25-DHCC Assay: Confirms Vitamin D deficiency.",
