      "Etiology": "- Primary: Overproduction and excessive endometrial release of prostaglandins, particularly **Prostaglandin F2-alpha (PGF2a)** and Prostaglandin E2 (PGE2), during endometrial desquamation.\n- Secondary: Endometriosis, uterine leiomyomas (fibroids), adenomyosis, pelvic infection, cervical stenosis, or intra-uterine devices (IUDs).",
