      "Etiology": "- Ovarian Diseases (Most Common): Polycystic Ovarian Syndrome (PCOS / Stein-Leventhal syndrome), premature ovarian insufficiency / perimenopause.\n- Endocrine Disruptions: Hyperthyroidism (increased thyroid hormone characteristically causes oligomenorrhea), hyperprolactinemia, Cushing's syndrome, congenital adrenal hyperplasia.\n- Functional / Hypothalamic Causes: Significant weight loss, extreme athletic training, job-related stress, severe emotional disturbance.\n- Physiological: Peri-pubertal transition (first 1–2 years following menarche) and perimenopause.",
