      "Definition": "A complex endocrine and metabolic disorder in women characterized by androgen excess, ovulatory dysfunction (oligomenorrhea or anovulation), and polycystic ovarian morphology.",
      "Normal Physiology": "In a normal menstrual cycle, pulsatile hypothalamic GnRH stimulates anterior pituitary secretion of FSH and LH. FSH promotes early follicular growth and granulosa cell aromatase activity, converting theca-derived androgens into estradiol. A single dominant follicle matures and releases an ovum following a mid-cycle LH surge.",
