      "Diagnostic / Physiological Tests": "- Pelvic Ultrasonography: Demonstrates classic \"string-of-pearls\" sign (12 or more peripheral antral follicles measuring 2–9 mm in enlarged ovaries).\n- Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT): Assesses co-existing insulin resistance and impaired glucose tolerance.\n- Dexamethasone Suppression Test: Helps differentiate ovarian from adrenal sources of androgen excess.",
      "Normal vs. Abnormal Values": "Normal LH-to-FSH ratio = 1:1; PCOS LH-to-FSH ratio = 2:1 to 3:1. Normal female testosterone = 15–70 ng/dL; PCOS testosterone = elevated (> 80–150 ng/dL).",
