      "Etiology": "1. Huntington's Disease: Autosomal dominant mutation on chromosome 4 (CAG trinucleotide repeat expansion in the HTT gene coding for huntingtin protein).\n2. Sydenham's Chorea: Autoimmune post-streptococcal cross-reactivity affecting basal ganglia neurons (Rheumatic Fever).\n3. Lesions of the Putamen / Caudate Nucleus: Multiple small vascular or ischemic lesions in the striatum.",
