      "Clinical Features / Signature Symptoms": "- **Ataxic / Drunken Gait:** Unsteady, staggering, wide-based gait.\n- **Dysmetria & Past-Pointing:** Inability to gauge distance; the limb overshoots or undershoots the target.\n- **Intention Tremor:** Kinetic tremor appearing during voluntary movement that oscillates and worsens as the target is approached.\n- **Dysdiadochokinesia / Adiadochokinesia:** Inability to perform rapid alternating movements (e.g., pronation and supination).\n- **Scanning Speech:** Dysarthric, staccato speech with jumbled vocalization and irregular syllable timing.\n- **Nystagmus:** Tremor of the eyeballs during off-center fixation due to damping failure in vestibulo-ocular pathways.\n- **Rebound Phenomenon (Holmes Rebound Sign):** Inability to stop an ongoing isometric contraction when resistance is suddenly removed.\n- **Hypotonia:** Reduced muscle tone and pendular deep tendon reflexes.",
