      "Normal Physiology": "The posterior parietal cortex (parieto-occipitotemporal association area) provides continuous analysis of the spatial coordinates of all parts of the body and its surroundings. It integrates visual input from the occipital cortex and somatosensory input from the parietal cortex. In right-handed individuals, the right (representational/non-dominant) parietal hemisphere controls spatial attention for both the left and right halves of space, whereas the left (dominant) hemisphere controls attention primarily for the right side.",
