      "Clinical Features / Signature Symptoms": "- **Personal Neglect:** Ignoring the left half of one's own body (dressing half the body, shaving half the face, washing one side).\n- **Extrapersonal / Spatial Neglect:** Ignoring objects, people, or food located on the left side (eating food only from the right half of a plate, reading only the right side of a page).\n- **Constructional Apraxia & Drawing Deficits:** Severe impairment when copying drawings; the patient completely omits the left side of drawings (e.g., drawing only the right half of a clock face or flower).\n- **Sensory Extinction:** Patient perceives a single stimulus on the left, but when bilateral simultaneous stimuli are delivered, the left-sided stimulus is ignored/extinguished.\n- **Anosognosia:** Lack of awareness or denial of their own spatial/motor deficit.",
