      "Definition": "A neurological condition resulting from a vascular lesion of the posterior thalamus, characterized by severe contralateral sensory impairment, loss of discriminative sensations, sensory ataxia, and severe, unprovoked central neuropathic pain (thalamic hyperpathia).",
      "Normal Physiology": "The ventral posterolateral (VPL) nucleus of the thalamus serves as the essential relay station for all somatosensory pathways—the dorsal column-medial lemniscal system and the spinothalamic tract—projecting to the primary somatosensory cortex (S-I). It also integrates dentatorubrothalamic inputs from the cerebellum and relays them to the motor cortex (areas 4 and 6) to coordinate voluntary movement.",
