      "Site": "Ventral posterolateral (VPL) nucleus and posterolateral nuclear group of the thalamus.",
      "Pathophysiology": "Ischemic destruction of the VPL nucleus interrupts third-order sensory neurons projecting to the somatosensory cortex. Deafferentation of thalamocortical networks leads to synaptic reorganization and autonomous hyperexcitability of surviving thalamic neurons. Deprived of normal inhibitory modulation from the thalamic reticular nucleus, these neurons generate spontaneous, chaotic burst discharges that reach the cortex, producing continuous central pain without peripheral noxious input.",
