      "Etiology": "1. Axial Hypermetropia (Most Common): Decreased antero-posterior axial length of the eyeball (short globe).\n2. Refractive / Curvature Hypermetropia: Abnormally flat cornea or weakened lens system (low refractive power).\n3. Aphakia: Absence of the crystalline lens (e.g., post-cataract extraction).",
      "Site": "Optical system of the eye (flattened cornea, weak lens, or shortened posterior scleral globe).",
