      "Equations / Relationships": "- Refractive Power ( P ) in Diopters = 1 / Focal Length ( f ) in meters.\n- Lens Correction: Corrected Power = Eye Power + Convex Lens Power.",
      "Differential Diagnosis": "Myopia (focal point in front of retina); Presbyopia (age-related sclerosal loss of lens elasticity in older adults, whereas hypermetropia is an anatomical refractive error present from youth); Astigmatism.",
      "Complications": "Accommodative esotropia (convergent squint), amblyopia ex anopsia (lazy eye in children if uncorrected), acute angle-closure glaucoma (due to shallow anterior chamber in short globes)."
