      "Diagnostic / Physiological Tests": "- Parallel Black Bars Astigmatic Chart: Patient views sets of parallel bars at different angular orientations; bars parallel to the out-of-focus cylindrical axis appear fuzzy, whereas perpendicular bars appear sharp.\n- Retinoscopy & Trial Lenses: Utilizes spherical and cylindrical trial lenses to identify the exact axis and dioptric strength of the cylindrical error.",
      "Graphs / Tracings": "Ray-diagram of an oblong astigmatic lens demonstrating light focusing at a shorter focal line for plane BD and a longer focal line for plane AC.",
