      "Functional Abnormality": "Progressive loss of lens dioptric accommodative capacity and recession of the near point of vision.",
      "Regulation / Feedback": "Parasympathetic signals to the ciliary muscle increase during near gaze attempts, but physical lens sclerosal rigidity prevents the required increase in dioptric power.",
