      "Physiological Basis of Features": "- Receding Near Point: Inability of the hardened lens to increase its dioptric power forces the nearest point of clear focus farther away from the eye.\n- Holding Objects Farther Away: Pushing objects away decreases the angle of light divergence, allowing light rays to focus closer to the retina despite reduced lens accommodative power.",
