      "Normal Physiology": "The membranous labyrinth is filled with endolymph, a potassium-rich fluid (resembling intracellular fluid) maintained at a high endocochlear potential (+80 to +85 mV) relative to perilymph by the stria vascularis. Endolymph bathes the sensory hair cells of both the cochlea and vestibular organs (utricle, saccule, semicircular canals).",
