      "Treatment + Physiological Basis": "- Symptomatic Management: Antiemetics and vestibular suppressants during acute attacks.\n- Dietary Fluid/Salt Restriction & Diuretics: Reduces endolymphatic volume and pressure.\n- Refractory Cases: Surgical labyrinthectomy or chemical ablation/vestibular nerve section to eliminate asymmetric vestibular inputs.",
      "Differential Diagnosis": "Benign Paroxysmal Positional Vertigo (BPPV; brief positional bursts without hearing loss); Acoustic Neuroma (progressive non-fluctuating loss); Labyrinthitis."
