      "Definition": "A physiological disorder occurring in susceptible individuals caused by repetitive, unaccustomed overstimulation of the vestibular apparatus during travel or motion.",
      "Normal Physiology": "Head movement causes fluid movement in the semicircular canals (angular acceleration) and statoconia displacement on macular hair cells in the utricle and saccule (linear acceleration). Hair cell depolarization transmits motion signals via Scarpa's ganglion and the 8th nerve to vestibular nuclei and the vestibulocerebellum (flocculonodular lobe) to coordinate posture and eye movements.",
