      "Sequence of Changes": "Ethmoid cribriform plate fracture / nasal mucosal edema -> Shearing of olfactory nerve fibers or nasal blockage -> Odorants fail to trigger receptor cell cAMP cascade -> No action potentials transmitted along CN I -> Complete loss of smell sensation (Anosmia).",
      "Clinical Features / Signature Symptoms": "Inability to perceive or identify familiar odors; apparent loss of food flavor perception; absence of olfactory autonomic reflexes (e.g., lack of cephalic phase salivation to pleasant food smells).",
