      "Diagnostic / Physiological Tests": "- Qualitative Clinical Testing: Individual closes eyes and blocks one nostril while familiar non-irritating odors (asafetida, clove oil, peppermint oil) are presented.\n- Quantitative Olfactometry: Measures exact detection thresholds for odoriferous substances (e.g., methyl mercaptan).",
      "Exceptions": "Irritating or pungent chemicals like ammonia, chlorine, menthol, or menthol-peppermint do **not** test olfaction (CN I) because they stimulate naked trigeminal (CN V) pain/nociceptive nerve endings in the nasal mucosa, eliciting burning sensations, lacrimation, or sneezing even in totally anosmic individuals.",
      "Differential Diagnosis": "Parosmia/Dysosmia (perverted smell seen in temporal lobe epilepsy / uncinate fits); Selective Odor Blindness (genetic lack of a specific receptor protein)."
